# SISAP 2026 Task 3 Developer Notes

**Team:** Seed 42
**Team ID:** 64

## Scope

This repository implements the SISAP 2026 Task 3 challenge: indexing very sparse high-dimensional vectors with memory-efficient methods under realistic hardware limits.

The benchmark uses Natural Questions with 2.68M documents and 30,522 sparse dimensions, encoded with SPLADE-v3 style learned sparse representations. The goal is approximate top-30 retrieval with average recall at or above 0.9.

## Final repository state

- The paper and experiment narrative are finalized in `report/paper.tex`.
- Final CSV summaries are stored in `report/final_csv_results/`.
- Final figures used to support the paper are stored in `report/final_figures/`.
- The implementation centers on the custom `InvertedBlock` structure with clustering, exact per-cluster summaries, inverted blocks, and query-time pruning.
- Search is controlled by `md`, `mqt`, `msb`, and `heap_factor`.

## Core executable

The main entry point is [src/main.cc](src/main.cc). It is responsible for the full end-to-end benchmark loop:

- parses the command line flags `--dataset`, `--task`, `--params`, `--input`, `--task-description`, and `--output`,
- resolves the dataset and task metadata,
- loads the selected JSON config set from `config/<folder>/`,
- reads the sparse HDF5 train/query arrays,
- runs clustering,
- builds exact per-cluster summary vectors,
- builds the partitioned inverted index,
- evaluates the search engine over all queries,
- computes Recall@30 and timing statistics,
- appends the metrics to the results CSV.

That file is the best place to inspect when changing how the benchmark is wired together or when adding a new execution mode.

## Final experiment runners

The final round-05 experiments are launched with the two scripts below.

- [scripts/run_static_exps_05_index.sh](scripts/run_static_exps_05_index.sh) builds the Docker image, runs the final index-building sweep `static_exps_05_index`, copies the generated CSV into the round-05 results folder, and generates the corresponding plots.
- [scripts/run_static_exps_05_search.sh](scripts/run_static_exps_05_search.sh) builds the Docker image, runs the final search sweep `static_exps_05_search`, and stores the resulting CSV and logs in the round-05 results folder.

These scripts are the canonical way to reproduce the final paper figures for the last experiment set.

## Plot scripts

- [scripts/static_exps_plots.py](scripts/static_exps_plots.py) generates the main static-experiment figures from the sweep CSVs. It supports the cluster-count sweep, the nb/nd sweep, and the three search-parameter sweeps (`md`, `mqt`, and `msb`). The script reads the CSVs, annotates the final index families, and writes publication-ready PNG figures.
- [scripts/static_exps_search_plots.py](scripts/static_exps_search_plots.py) is the search-only plotting helper used for the final result tables. It focuses on the `md`, `mqt`, and `msb` sweeps over the selected static index families and produces the plots stored in [report/final_figures](report/final_figures).

## What the final experiments show

- Index-building sweeps identify a compact family of usable structures, including the nine final configurations I-1 to I-9.
- The restricted index setups preserve recall while avoiding unnecessary growth in block fan-out and document budget.
- `md` is the primary global recall-latency control.
- `msb` is the main secondary control and saturates around 150 in the final sweeps.
- `mqt` is a weaker efficiency control once enough high-weight query terms are included.

